# Recorded from a second runtime; see docs/reference-runtime.md. The model is
# NOT committed -- see docs/fixture-provenance.md. No mandatory test reads
# this file.
#
# The vector below is what llama.cpp produced for this prompt, pooled and at
# unit length. It is recorded whole rather than sampled, because a cosine
# taken over part of a vector says nothing about the rest and the two faults
# this comparison found moved every component:
#
#   A WordPiece text is wrapped in [CLS] and [SEP] by construction. This
#   file states bos_token_id and eos_token_id and neither flag, and absent
#   was read as "the model does not say" -- six tokens to a model trained on
#   eight, cosine 0.994 and nothing refused.
#
#   nomic-bert splits its rotation. It had been written pairing element i
#   with its neighbour, from a recollection. Cosine 0.947.
#
# Neither was visible to 857,184 sweep comparisons, because the engine, the
# fixture and the independent implementation were all written from one
# reading of one description. This one was not.
#
# The weights are F16 on purpose. Against the Q8_0 file the two differ by
# 0.0026, and that difference is the other runtime's: ggml quantizes the
# activations to eight bits before every dot product against a quantized
# weight, and reads GELU from a table indexed and stored in f16 whose own
# worst error is 0.002 an activation. On F16 weights there is no such step
# and the two agree to 8.1e-05, which is accumulation order. The tolerance
# below is set from that measurement.

runtime llama.cpp e85caa8
model nomic-embed-text-v1.5.f16.gguf
prompt a cat sits on the mat
pooling mean
tolerance 5.0E-04

